<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name      "crowdsec-unraid-bouncer">
<!ENTITY author    "Railline">
<!ENTITY version   "2026.08.22.1">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Railline/unraid-community-apps/main/plugins/crowdsec-unraid-bouncer.plg">
<!ENTITY support   "https://github.com/Railline/unraid-community-apps/issues">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" pluginURL="&pluginURL;" support="&support;" min="6.9.0" icon="crowdsec-unraid-bouncer.png">

<CHANGES>
## crowdsec-unraid-bouncer

### 2026.08.22.1
- Keep the plugin focused exclusively on enforcing CrowdSec decisions by removing the unrelated firewall-drop export integration.
- Track every CrowdSec decision ID independently so overlapping decisions cannot prematurely unblock an address.
- Preserve active protection while switching between direct iptables and ipset backends.
- Remove managed firewall state when the service is stopped or disabled.
- Fix synchronization temporary-file cleanup and incorporate the correction proposed in pull request 3.
- Validate stream JSON, runtime configuration, firewall identifiers, URLs, numeric limits, and incoming IPv4 values before applying changes.
- Harden daemon PID handling, API-key creation, WebUI input handling, CSRF form submission, response rendering, and configuration writes.
- Move volatile health and decision state off the flash drive and improve health consistency checks.
- Normalize duplicate or misplaced firewall jumps and repair backend-specific stale rules.
- Reduce idle log writes and add bounded retry backoff after synchronization failures.
- Simplify settings, labels, actions, status output, documentation, and package generation.

### 2026.07.14.1
- Add configurable CrowdSec LAPI stream timeout for large Global shield synchronizations.
- Add health monitoring, Unraid notifications, optional Telegram alerts, and recovery notifications.
- Restore persistent ipset package bootstrap for Global shield.
- Add a Community Applications compatible settings page and icon.

### 2026.05.11.13
- Deduplicate CrowdSec jumps and keep them as the first protected-chain rule.
- Detect duplicate or misplaced CrowdSec jumps during health checks.

### 2026.05.11.12
- Start the daemon in a detached session.

### 2026.05.11.11
- Fix WebUI configuration saves and preserve the API key when its field is left empty.

### 2026.05.11.8
- Add periodic full stream synchronization.

### 2026.05.11.6
- Load Global shield through a temporary ipset and swap it into place.
- Ignore IPv6 stream decisions until an IPv6 backend is available.

### 2026.05.11.4
- Use batched ipset restore for large Global shield updates.

### 2026.05.11.3
- Add Essential, Global, and Custom protection modes.
- Add auto, direct iptables, and ipset firewall backends.

### 2026.05.11.2
- Use the CrowdSec Local API bouncer stream.
- Add LAPI key and origin settings plus a direct-rule safety limit.

### 2026.05.11
- Initial release protecting host and Docker-published traffic.
</CHANGES>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE><![CDATA[
set -eu

NAME="crowdsec-unraid-bouncer"
BOOT_DIR="/boot/config/plugins/${NAME}"
WEB_DIR="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/${NAME}"
IPSET_PKG="${BOOT_DIR}/packages/ipset-7.15-x86_64-1.txz"
IPSET_URL="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Railline/unraid-community-apps/main/packages/ipset-7.15-x86_64-1.txz"
IPSET_SHA256="c190f4347e1ca429da27d95c0e393eb336b253cd3e5c73802deb69661fcdf41a"

mkdir -p "${BOOT_DIR}/packages" "${WEB_DIR}/include" /usr/local/sbin /etc/rc.d

if ! command -v ipset >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  if [ -f "$IPSET_PKG" ] && [ "$(sha256sum "$IPSET_PKG" | awk '{print $1}')" != "$IPSET_SHA256" ]; then
    echo "Removing an invalid cached ipset package" >&2
    rm -f "$IPSET_PKG"
  fi
  if [ ! -f "$IPSET_PKG" ]; then
    IPSET_DOWNLOAD="${IPSET_PKG}.download.$$"
    trap 'rm -f "$IPSET_DOWNLOAD"' EXIT
    if command -v curl >/dev/null 2>&1; then
      curl -fL --retry 3 --connect-timeout 10 "$IPSET_URL" -o "$IPSET_DOWNLOAD"
    elif command -v wget >/dev/null 2>&1; then
      wget -qO "$IPSET_DOWNLOAD" "$IPSET_URL"
    else
      echo "ipset is missing and neither curl nor wget is available" >&2
      exit 1
    fi
    if [ "$(sha256sum "$IPSET_DOWNLOAD" | awk '{print $1}')" != "$IPSET_SHA256" ]; then
      echo "Downloaded ipset package checksum mismatch" >&2
      exit 1
    fi
    mv "$IPSET_DOWNLOAD" "$IPSET_PKG"
    trap - EXIT
  fi
  installpkg "$IPSET_PKG"
  command -v ipset >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo "ipset installation failed" >&2; exit 1; }
fi

base64 -d > /usr/local/sbin/crowdsec-unraid-bouncer <<'B64_BIN'
